{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "**Cherry Blossoms and City Lights: A Whirlwind Week in Japan**\n\nLanding in Tokyo felt like stepping into a living postcard. The first morning I wandered through Shibuya Crossing, mesmerized by the sea of people moving in perfect sync. A quick espresso at a tiny café tucked beneath the neon signs gave me the fuel to explore Harajuku’s quirky boutiques, where vintage kimonos shared shelf space with avant‑garde streetwear.\n\nDay two took me to the tranquil Meiji Shrine, where the towering torii gate framed a whisper‑quiet forest despite the bustling city just beyond its walls. Afterward, I hopped on the Shinkansen to Kyoto, the bullet train’s smooth glide making the three‑hour flight feel like a breeze.\n\nIn Kyoto, I lost myself among the vermilion tunnels of Fushimi Inari Shrine, each gate a promise of good fortune. The afternoon was spent sipping matcha in a centuries‑old tea house, the bitter sweetness perfectly complementing the delicate wagashi served alongside. Evening brought a stroll through Gion, where I caught a fleeting glimpse of a geisha hurrying to her appointment, her silk kimono a flash of color against the stone lanes.\n\nA day trip to Nara introduced me to friendly deer that bowed for crackers, and the awe‑inspiring Todaiji Temple housing a giant bronze Buddha. The final night back in Tokyo was spent in Shinjuku’s Golden Gai, where tiny bars each told their own story over tiny glasses of whiskey and lively chatter.\n\nJapan’s blend of ancient tradition and cutting‑edge modernity left me humming with inspiration—already dreaming of the next ramen bowl, temple bell, and neon‑lit adventure.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.18877705931663513}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.0018999397289007902}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.08594398200511932}, {"token": " write", "logprob": -0.6126118302345276}, {"token": " a", "lo